Z||000000||rogergarrison||10-22-2000||11:09 AM||||<BR>Has anyone dealt with Twin Lakes Fiero in Illinois. Any problems with them anyone know of?<P>Im looking for someone in the Ohio area to R&R my 86 SE 4speed (410) for preferably 4 speed automatic. I want turn key job, ie) shifter,linkages, axles, flywheel, transaxle, addon oil cooler and anything else needed where I can drop it off, pick it up finished. Installer can keep 4 speed manual, Ferrari style shifter, slave clutch assby, clutch (recent)  any of the old parts he wants. It all works perfectly, including the slave cylinder. I just want to go to automatic. I may consider 3 speed automatic. Email me with your number, price. Im just to busy in my business to take all the necessary time to do the job myself. Im in Columbus, ohio. The closer you are the better too. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Old Lar||10-22-2000||12:17 PM||||Twin Lakes has done a lot of work for me..all quality work.  Bob is putting a T440 (4 speed automatic in my 88GT).  It is a brand new transmission.||||reg||14
Z||000002||rogergarrison||10-22-2000||05:10 PM||||thanks Lar. If I dont find someone closer that does top notch work, ill probably call him to set it up. I demand a quality job, ive put over $30 k in this Ferrari kit and plan on keeping it till i die. Everyone knowlegable says the automatic ought to have even better performance than the 4 speed - and told the turbo in it will work lots better held wide open with it as opposed to dropping rpm shifting manual, Thanks again, let us know how yours turns out too.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Rodney||10-22-2000||08:19 PM||||The turbo may work better on an automatic but my 88 Mera was an automatic when I bought it and I swapped to the Getrag 5 speed. A automatic in a Ferrari replica is a bummer in my opinion! Just my opinion though. I love my 5 speed and how you get to play with it. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||10-22-2000||08:52 PM||||hi Rodney! Btw, the Ferrari enameled pins worked great for dash and rear view mirrors. Ive played with the manual transmission enough now, lol. Im getting too old to mess with it now. I just want the auto for laid back fast cruising now. You do know that you can get real Ferraris now with 'automatics' the F1 style is used in new models as an option and Porsche too. Im just thinking wouldnt it be too cool to use a late model electronic transmission and making the steering wheel paddles to manually shift it if you wanted -----mmmmmmmmmm? <P>Roger||||reg||1
